  "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
  "label": "User projected onto the textual message as the target of blame",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the textual material ('your stupid government') which uses the deictic 'your' to directly address the viewer, making the user the recipient of the blame being directed at the government. This creates a semiotic projection where the user is positioned as the one whose government is being criticized, thereby implicating them in the scapegoating narrative. The projection is onto the text_chunk, which contains the phrase 'your stupid government', making the user feel personally targeted by the meme's message.",
